    "html": "<p>A sound wave of frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"170\\text{ Hz}\"></span> travels through air at a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"340\\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span>. Two points, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, are separated by a distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\\text{ m}\"></span> along the direction of energy transfer. What is the phase difference between the oscillations at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi\\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\\pi\\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
